      "sourceTextSha256": "f4bd617041568d1eb1c054baf33e6096838a91c1c7fd57a84f550a181dcb879e",
      "text": "The Guayabero River and Cajuche Spring",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-mw8vsjy6-afdp41bp",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      }
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "626dabd4f66419f731b9040c36ff633e8743302003db4394c2fa3bd635465687",
      "text": "After breakfast, take a boat trip along the Guayabero River. The river runs through the national park, and the boat ride gives you a view of the region’s natural landscapes.\n\nAfter the boat ride, switch to 4×4 pickup trucks. The drive to the area around Cajuche Spring takes about 20 minutes, and you’ll continue on foot from there.\n\nA traditional lunch wrapped in Bijagos banana leaves is planned during the excursion.\n\nReturn to La Macarena after the excursion. In the evening, get to know local folklore and regional cooking through music, conversation with young residents and dinner. Dinner is included.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-mw8vsjy6-afdp41bp",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      }
    }
